WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
Nickel goes into stainless steel
and electric-vehicle batteries.

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:10.150
In January 2020, Indonesia reinstated
its ban on exports of raw nickel ore,

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.290
two years earlier than announced.

4
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:19.690
In 2019, Indonesia mined about 800,000
tonnes of a world total of 2.7 million.

5
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:26.410
By 2025: 2.6 million of 3.9
million, USGS estimates.

6
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.590
Who gains when a country closes a door?

7
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.590
Only Indonesia?

8
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.650
Only foreign mining companies?

9
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.110
Or do trade bans always fail?

10
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.810
In this mission, you'll separate
protectionism from resource nationalism.

11
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.270
Then you'll trace the ban's
effects beyond Indonesia,

12
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.970
and follow the European Union's case
to the World Trade Organization.

13
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.710
Your mission: find out who gains when
Indonesia closes the door to raw nickel

14
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.760
exports.
